{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792125607,"nonce":"haVWQd492lb7E1HjDba6qOCiX1w=","message":"Decision: [fetch.hosts.\"\u003chost\u003e\"] rps (0 \u003c rps \u003c= 2) matches the exact hostname only, case-insensitive, port ignored, no subdomain matching; it replaces both default_rps and a source's own rate_limit for that host; robots Crawl-delay stays a floor and 429/Retry-After holds still apply. Built-in defaults nlx.jobsyn.org and usnlx.com at 1 rps (robots allows, no Crawl-delay, no 429s seen); user entries merge over the built-ins rather than replacing the table, so to slow a built-in back down set its rps. Keys must be bare hostnames (no scheme, port, path, wildcard); validator messages are value-free per the config_watch rule. fetch.hosts is reloadable and its /config/changes value shows only 'changed'. Reason: exact match is least surprising and cannot accidentally speed up unrelated subdomains; the user's per-host choice is explicit, so it beats per-source defaults; merging keeps the NLX speedup when the user adds another host.","files":null}]}